 694:Core/Src/main.c ****  * and pushes them as one frame; drops the whole batch if the FIFO is full.
 695:Core/Src/main.c ****  *
 696:Core/Src/main.c ****  * seq is advanced only on a successful push, which is what lets the host tell
 697:Core/Src/main.c ****  * the two loss modes apart: a FIFO overflow here leaves seq contiguous but
 698:Core/Src/main.c ****  * slower than wall-clock, while bytes lost on the wire leave holes in seq.
